{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01A9AA1C63RDrnAgjC3cqskJ","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/private/tmp/trial-pi-97-fsmtmhyh/.xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_metric.py","content":"import xorq.operators as xo\nfrom xorq.utils import FrozenDict\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfm_df = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con=None,\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\n)\n\n# Read census data\ncensus_df = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con=None,\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\n)\n\n# Sum all farmers markets from all states\nfm_total = fm_df[\"farmers_markets\"].sum()\n\n# Get US total population (first row of census data is the US total)\ncensus_us = census_df[census_df[\"NAME\"] == \"United States\"]\nus_population = census_us[\"POPESTIMATE2025\"].iloc[0]\n\n# Create output with the metric\nexpr = xo.pd.DataFrame({\n    \"total_farmers_markets\": [fm_total],\n    \"us_population\": [us_population],\n    \"farmers_markets_per_100k\": [(fm_total / us_population) * 100000]\n})\n"}}}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! The census file has:\n- `NAME` column with state/region names\n- `POPESTIMATE2025` column with 2025 population estimates\n\nThe file structure shows the first row is \"United States\" which is the total U.S. population we need: 341,784,857.\n\nNow I can write a proper build script that:\n1. Reads the farmers markets data\n2. Gets the total farmers markets count\n3. Gets the U.S. total population from the census data\n4. Calculates the ratio\n\nLet me write the correct script.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll create a proper build script that reads both datasets and calculates the metric:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01A9AA1C63RDrnAgjC3cqskJ","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/private/tmp/trial-pi-97-fsmtmhyh/.xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_metric.py","content":"import xorq.operators as xo\nfrom xorq.utils import FrozenDict\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfm_df = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con=None,\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\n)\n\n# Read census data\ncensus_df = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con=None,\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\n)\n\n# Sum all farmers markets from all states\nfm_total = fm_df[\"farmers_markets\"].sum()\n\n# Get US total population (first row of census data is the US total)\ncensus_us = census_df[census_df[\"NAME\"] == \"United States\"]\nus_population = census_us[\"POPESTIMATE2025\"].iloc[0]\n\n# Create output with the metric\nexpr = xo.pd.DataFrame({\n    \"total_farmers_markets\": [fm_total],\n    \"us_population\": [us_population],\n    \"farmers_markets_per_100k\": [(fm_total / us_population) * 100000]\n})\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provide